        "original_id": "d694c3a2-efb9-5a57-9115-8871c3fa545a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fetteresso Castle, Cowie Castle, Catterline, Aberdeenshire, Scotland\n- Topics: Architecture, historic sites, prehistoric use\n\nFacts:\n- Fetteresso Castle is a 14th-century towerhouse.\n- The site of Fetteresso Castle shows clear evidence of prehistoric use.\n- Fetteresso Castle was rebuilt in 1761 as a Scottish gothic style Palladian manor.\n- Cowie Castle is a ruined fortress in Aberdeenshire, Scotland.\n- Catterline is in a general area that includes Fetteresso Castle, Fiddes Castle, the Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, and Muchalls Castle as noted architectural or historic features.",
